{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description","id":1533399,"title":"How would you rewrite the original Giovanni clan description?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-30T17:50:44-07:00","id":1533399,"title":"How would you rewrite the original Giovanni clan description?","content":"The Giovanni were introduced in the first edition Players Guide which was then reprinted verbatim in the second edition Vampire Players Guide. It had all the basics of the clan as we know it, but things were left purposefully vague. Likely because the history of Clan Giovanni was to be revealed slowly in the subsequent Giovanni Chronicles and other sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> Eventually we got the name of their earlier clan, the Cappadocians; the history of the Cappadocian clan in broad strokes in their Dark Ages clanbook; and confirmation that a whole lot of Cappadocians had actually survived the Giovanni purge to the extend their claims of wiping out the other members of their clan was just ridiculous.<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;mystery&quot; behind the Giovanni were very much a PLAYER mystery, in terms of what we as players would learn in the course of several years of real life gaming releases, and much less a CHARACTER mystery in terms of what vampires probably knew or at least perspective from centuries of knowledge. So basically, how would you rewrite the original Giovanni clan description in order to accurately describe the clan as it <i>should</i> have been known back in 1991. <br /> <br /> Which is that the Giovanni family is dominant since Augustus is recognized as the clan's eldest, but that all of these surviving Cappadocians - the Samedi, the Lamia, various Cappadocians that survived the purge, and possibly ancient and elder Cappadocians long thought dead but could possibly be stirring? Obviously you can't refer to FUTURE events (future in the sense of occurring post 1991). Likewise there can still be some mysteries left to reveal, but no more than any other clan has. So explicit mentions of things like the Harbingers waking up is forbidden, though such mysteries can be hinted at to give inspiration to the STs. Those canonical events in whatever editions may or may not happen. It's just what the status quo should have been reveled back in 1991.<br /> <br /> So it's basically describing what is now called the Hecata except 1) no Nagaraja because they aren't actually part of that clan, and 2) the Giovanni are still seen as in head of it. The idea is to provide enough so that a player wanting to create a &quot;Giovanni&quot; clan character in 1991 can do so regardless if they are Giovanni or one of their allied families like the Dunsirn, be Samedi, a surviving lineage from Lord Camden or anyone else, and so on.<br /> <br /> So no more than around 800-1000 words for the whole shebang - general description, nickname, appearance, haven, backgrounds, character creation, disciplines, weaknesses, etc. One requirement is that all these bloodlines should be treated mechanically the same - they all have the same weaknesses and disciplines instead of the variety they originally had. Customization of specific lineages can always be done through appropriate Flaws IMO.<br /> <br /> How would you do it? I've tried writing it myself, but always overshoot the word limit by a lot. I just try to include too much detail and haven't yet figured out a way to make things succinct but interesting.<br /> <br /> Hoping people will be interested and that we can see some really inspiring examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T19:47:27-07:00","id":1533401,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it would be rough for me, because I disagree with the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil compared to &quot;common&quot; Disciplines like Presence and Dominate. That's an idea that works in DnD, not in VTM. And that, imo, flawed idea is extremely central to the Giovanni. If, like myself, you don't accept the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil, then you either have to come up with a reason for the Giovanni to be especially evil that isn't rooted in Necromancy, or jettison the idea that they are a special kind of evil.<br /> <br /> Several ideas come to mind, but all of them overlap heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, and Baali. You could make them a Rated R Addams Family, but that overlaps heavily with the Tzims. You could make them the economic power behind Italy, but that heavily overlaps with the Ventrue. You could make their occultism outright demonic, but that heavily overlaps with the Baali.<br /> <br /> I guess you could make them scattered mercenaries who do Necromancy work for pay/boons. Kind of overlaps with the Ravnos, but not to nearly as breakingly a degree as the others. Yeah, scattered mercenaries who usually do things like holding real seances for the living, and using information learned from the dead to con humans. Players would find them hustling humans and pay them to do something Necromancy related. Yeah, Ravnos+Necromancy could work as a reinvention of the Giovanni. Anything else overlaps so heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, or Baali that it's like, why bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T23:25:37-07:00","id":1533412,"title":"","content":"Alright, I\u2019m taking a shot at it. This was a little bit rushed, with more time i would probably change a few things. I think if i were making the Giovanni from scratch, I would have selected a name that sounds more like a surname from Medieval Venice rather than the Italian version of John. That is why I have an asterisk with Giovanni. Maybe Rosellini? Anyway, i am keeping it as Giovanni now for the purposes of this exercise. I went a little bit over 1000 words, but I\u2019m still in the neighborhood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clan Hecata</b><br /> <br /> The Hecata have had a long history as a Clan of scholars and mystics, studying the mysteries of death, not only physical death and the vampiric condition, but also the spirits of the dead. These necromancers did more than study death, they looked for purpose in unlife and members of the Hecata were prominent in cults and religious movements, using their connections to the departed to unlock long forgotten mysteries. Traditionally more arcane and intellectual than political, the Clan had a long history of neutrality in the world of kindred schemes and conflicts. This would begin change in the Middle Ages with the rise of what would become the Hecata\u2019s most prominent faction.<br /> <br /> At some point in the Middle Ages, a family of Venetian Necromancers was embraced into Clan Hecata. At the time, this mortal family was already centuries old and were masters of Necromancy to rival even the elders of Clan Hecata. The Giovanni* family, with their powerful necromantic magic, financial acumen, and fierce loyalty would soon come to dominate the Hecata Clan. While the more fractured and independent Hecata pursued their mystical arts largely independently, the Giovanni family worked together to advance their already considerable knowledge, used their mystic arts in combination with their vampiric abilities to accumulate wealth and power, and embraced only within their own mortal family.<br /> <br /> Within several centuries, the Giovanni family was by far the most powerful faction within the Hecata, so much so that other factions tried to resist their rise to power and were defeated by the still young and relatively tiny necromancer family. The nascent Camarilla, wary of the Giovanni\u2019s rapid rise in power and fearful that this group of relative neonates might join the Anarchs, sought to curtail their ascent. After a relatively brief conflict, the Giovanni agreed to remain neutral in all kindred affairs, an agreement known as the Promise of 1528. Since that time, the Giovanni have grown in wealth and temporal power, but have stayed true to their promise of staying out of vampiric politics. It is rumored that this promise has an expiration date, that it was intended to last 500 years and that in the early decades of the next millennium (its 1991 now) the Giovanni will be free to take a more active hand in vampiric affairs.<br /> <br /> For centuries the Giovanni have embraced only from their own family, with young Giovanni mortals trained from childhood to become necromancers and eventually, if they prove themselves, vampires. The Giovanni are known not only to keep their vampiric blood in the family, but have long practiced incest as well. As time passed, the family has become more inbred, more perverse and dark, further removed from humanity - if they were ever that human to begin with. Rumors abound about the twisted upbringing Giovanni youth are subjected to and the dark rituals they use to commune with or control the dead. Perhaps more than any other group, the Giovanni are secretive, mysterious, and insular. The family has at its disposal both immense mystical and financial power, as its long policy of neutrality has allowed them to amass both in relative peace. It isn\u2019t uncommon for members of the Giovanni family to occasionally make deals with other kindred - loans, revealing information known only to the dead, business deals, selling secrets. Almost without exception, the Giovanni honor their contracts and agreements, though their sinister reputation makes many kindred deal with them reluctantly.<br /> <br /> In modern nights, when most kindred think of the Hecata, they think of the Giovanni family. Other factions and individuals are scattered across the world, sometimes even powerful elders, but in influence and notoriety they pale in comparison to the Giovanni family, small as they may be.<br /> <br /> There are several other factions within the Hecata that are somewhat well known. One are the Cappadocians, perhaps the largest group within the Clan even including the Giovanni. The Cappadocians are known as religious scholars and mystics, largely apolitical who keep to themselves and, despite their relatively high numbers and greater age, maintain a low profile. The Lamia are another well known group, a mostly female cult dedicated to Lilith, some say that that they served the Clan founder in ancient days. Now the Lamia are largely extinct. The Samedi are hideously ugly, so close to death itself that their appearance is that of a fetid corpse. There are numerous other tiny groups of Hecata around the world, some well established, other merely rumor, though none can compare to the Giovanni in influence or notoriety.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames</b>: Necromancers<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: Members of the Giovanni family all come from from a single Venetian family, and are almost always caucasians with dark hair and brown eyes. The Giovanni also tend to have a distinct appearance, a certain similarity in features that arose from inbreeding over the generations. Some also have physical deformities as a result. The Giovanni tend to dress in conservative and formal styles, expensive suits or elegant dresses. Other Hecata vampires are far more diverse in appearance, both ethnically and in terms of attire. The Samedi, all having the appearance of rotten corpses, usually care little for style, save for clothing that may hide their hideousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven</b>: The Giovanni family maintain several opulent estates around the world, usually if there is a Giovanni presence in a city, there will be such an estate. When only one or two Giovanni are in a location, they usually have a mansion or luxury building in which to sleep and they often have other properties - graveyards, abandoned hospitals, or other such locations to practice unwholesome rituals. Cappadcoians favor much more humble dwelling where they can maintain their privacy, though they too prefer a location where they have access to the dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Members of Giovanni are all homeschooled, taught about the supernatural from a young age and trained in the dark arts as well as receiving an education on finance, politics, and other practical subjects. Most spent years as ghouls before being embraced. Cappadocians come from more scholarly or religious backgrounds - professors, priests, philosophers, doctors.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation</b>: in most cases mental attributes are primary, Giovanni nearly always have high resources unless some misfortune has befallen them.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Auspex, Fortitude, Necromancy. Different Hecata factions tend to favor different out of Clan disciplines - Obfuscate for the Samedi being the most common along with Dominate for the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> <b>Weaknesses</b>: being closer to death than other vampires, the kiss of the Hecata drains the life from victims as well as the blood, inflicting 2 levels of damage for each blood point drained.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: the Giovanni are strictly organized, ruled by the patriarch of the mortal family, now an elder vampire, often with vampires obeying the commands of their sire who is also a mortal mother or father. Other factions within the Clan have little in the way of organization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T06:31:48-07:00","id":1533415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533401#post1533401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it would be rough for me, because I disagree with the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil compared to &quot;common&quot; Disciplines like Presence and Dominate. That's an idea that works in DnD, not in VTM. And that, imo, flawed idea is extremely central to the Giovanni. If, like myself, you don't accept the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil, then you either have to come up with a reason for the Giovanni to be especially evil that isn't rooted in Necromancy, or jettison the idea that they are a special kind of evil.<br /> <br /> Several ideas come to mind, but all of them overlap heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, and Baali. You could make them a Rated R Addams Family, but that overlaps heavily with the Tzims. You could make them the economic power behind Italy, but that heavily overlaps with the Ventrue. You could make their occultism outright demonic, but that heavily overlaps with the Baali.<br /> <br /> I guess you could make them scattered mercenaries who do Necromancy work for pay/boons. Kind of overlaps with the Ravnos, but not to nearly as breakingly a degree as the others. Yeah, scattered mercenaries who usually do things like holding real seances for the living, and using information learned from the dead to con humans. Players would find them hustling humans and pay them to do something Necromancy related. Yeah, Ravnos+Necromancy could work as a reinvention of the Giovanni. Anything else overlaps so heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, or Baali that it's like, why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but the problem with necromancy in this case, wasn't it the way the Giovanni treated the dead as mere tools? And in some cases they still tormented them as fun or even as punishment for keeping a soul trapped in the earthly world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T06:37:40-07:00","id":1533417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533412#post1533412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I\u2019m taking a shot at it. This was a little bit rushed, with more time i would probably change a few things. I think if i were making the Giovanni from scratch, I would have selected a name that sounds more like a surname from Medieval Venice rather than the Italian version of John. That is why I have an asterisk with Giovanni. Maybe Rosellini? Anyway, i am keeping it as Giovanni now for the purposes of this exercise. I went a little bit over 1000 words, but I\u2019m still in the neighborhood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clan Hecata</b><br /> <br /> The Hecata have had a long history as a Clan of scholars and mystics, studying the mysteries of death, not only physical death and the vampiric condition, but also the spirits of the dead. These necromancers did more than study death, they looked for purpose in unlife and members of the Hecata were prominent in cults and religious movements, using their connections to the departed to unlock long forgotten mysteries. Traditionally more arcane and intellectual than political, the Clan had a long history of neutrality in the world of kindred schemes and conflicts. This would begin change in the Middle Ages with the rise of what would become the Hecata\u2019s most prominent faction.<br /> <br /> At some point in the Middle Ages, a family of Venetian Necromancers was embraced into Clan Hecata. At the time, this mortal family was already centuries old and were masters of Necromancy to rival even the elders of Clan Hecata. The Giovanni* family, with their powerful necromantic magic, financial acumen, and fierce loyalty would soon come to dominate the Hecata Clan. While the more fractured and independent Hecata pursued their mystical arts largely independently, the Giovanni family worked together to advance their already considerable knowledge, used their mystic arts in combination with their vampiric abilities to accumulate wealth and power, and embraced only within their own mortal family.<br /> <br /> Within several centuries, the Giovanni family was by far the most powerful faction within the Hecata, so much so that other factions tried to resist their rise to power and were defeated by the still young and relatively tiny necromancer family. The nascent Camarilla, wary of the Giovanni\u2019s rapid rise in power and fearful that this group of relative neonates might join the Anarchs, sought to curtail their ascent. After a relatively brief conflict, the Giovanni agreed to remain neutral in all kindred affairs, an agreement known as the Promise of 1528. Since that time, the Giovanni have grown in wealth and temporal power, but have stayed true to their promise of staying out of vampiric politics. It is rumored that this promise has an expiration date, that it was intended to last 500 years and that in the early decades of the next millennium (its 1991 now) the Giovanni will be free to take a more active hand in vampiric affairs.<br /> <br /> For centuries the Giovanni have embraced only from their own family, with young Giovanni mortals trained from childhood to become necromancers and eventually, if they prove themselves, vampires. The Giovanni are known not only to keep their vampiric blood in the family, but have long practiced incest as well. As time passed, the family has become more inbred, more perverse and dark, further removed from humanity - if they were ever that human to begin with. Rumors abound about the twisted upbringing Giovanni youth are subjected to and the dark rituals they use to commune with or control the dead. Perhaps more than any other group, the Giovanni are secretive, mysterious, and insular. The family has at its disposal both immense mystical and financial power, as its long policy of neutrality has allowed them to amass both in relative peace. It isn\u2019t uncommon for members of the Giovanni family to occasionally make deals with other kindred - loans, revealing information known only to the dead, business deals, selling secrets. Almost without exception, the Giovanni honor their contracts and agreements, though their sinister reputation makes many kindred deal with them reluctantly.<br /> <br /> In modern nights, when most kindred think of the Hecata, they think of the Giovanni family. Other factions and individuals are scattered across the world, sometimes even powerful elders, but in influence and notoriety they pale in comparison to the Giovanni family, small as they may be.<br /> <br /> There are several other factions within the Hecata that are somewhat well known. One are the Cappadocians, perhaps the largest group within the Clan even including the Giovanni. The Cappadocians are known as religious scholars and mystics, largely apolitical who keep to themselves and, despite their relatively high numbers and greater age, maintain a low profile. The Lamia are another well known group, a mostly female cult dedicated to Lilith, some say that that they served the Clan founder in ancient days. Now the Lamia are largely extinct. The Samedi are hideously ugly, so close to death itself that their appearance is that of a fetid corpse. There are numerous other tiny groups of Hecata around the world, some well established, other merely rumor, though none can compare to the Giovanni in influence or notoriety.<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames</b>: Necromancers<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b>: Members of the Giovanni family all come from from a single Venetian family, and are almost always caucasians with dark hair and brown eyes. The Giovanni also tend to have a distinct appearance, a certain similarity in features that arose from inbreeding over the generations. Some also have physical deformities as a result. The Giovanni tend to dress in conservative and formal styles, expensive suits or elegant dresses. Other Hecata vampires are far more diverse in appearance, both ethnically and in terms of attire. The Samedi, all having the appearance of rotten corpses, usually care little for style, save for clothing that may hide their hideousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Haven</b>: The Giovanni family maintain several opulent estates around the world, usually if there is a Giovanni presence in a city, there will be such an estate. When only one or two Giovanni are in a location, they usually have a mansion or luxury building in which to sleep and they often have other properties - graveyards, abandoned hospitals, or other such locations to practice unwholesome rituals. Cappadcoians favor much more humble dwelling where they can maintain their privacy, though they too prefer a location where they have access to the dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Members of Giovanni are all homeschooled, taught about the supernatural from a young age and trained in the dark arts as well as receiving an education on finance, politics, and other practical subjects. Most spent years as ghouls before being embraced. Cappadocians come from more scholarly or religious backgrounds - professors, priests, philosophers, doctors.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation</b>: in most cases mental attributes are primary, Giovanni nearly always have high resources unless some misfortune has befallen them.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan Disciplines</b>: Auspex, Fortitude, Necromancy. Different Hecata factions tend to favor different out of Clan disciplines - Obfuscate for the Samedi being the most common along with Dominate for the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> <b>Weaknesses</b>: being closer to death than other vampires, the kiss of the Hecata drains the life from victims as well as the blood, inflicting 2 levels of damage for each blood point drained.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: the Giovanni are strictly organized, ruled by the patriarch of the mortal family, now an elder vampire, often with vampires obeying the commands of their sire who is also a mortal mother or father. Other factions within the Clan have little in the way of organization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You did a good job there, I just found this part of them limiting themselves to their own family a bit forced, I find it a bit difficult to believe that the Hecata would be able to stop their members from embracing those who come from outside, the Giovanni's &quot;poison&quot; did much more sense. One idea would be to place this &quot;poison&quot; of the Giovanni as part of the promise of 1528, a guarantee that the clan would not embrace haphazardly and become enormous over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T08:35:59-07:00","id":1533418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533401#post1533401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it would be rough for me, because I disagree with the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil compared to &quot;common&quot; Disciplines like Presence and Dominate. That's an idea that works in DnD, not in VTM. And that, imo, flawed idea is extremely central to the Giovanni. If, like myself, you don't accept the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil, then you either have to come up with a reason for the Giovanni to be especially evil that isn't rooted in Necromancy, or jettison the idea that they are a special kind of evil.<br /> <br /> Several ideas come to mind, but all of them overlap heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, and Baali. You could make them a Rated R Addams Family, but that overlaps heavily with the Tzims. You could make them the economic power behind Italy, but that heavily overlaps with the Ventrue. You could make their occultism outright demonic, but that heavily overlaps with the Baali.<br /> <br /> I guess you could make them scattered mercenaries who do Necromancy work for pay/boons. Kind of overlaps with the Ravnos, but not to nearly as breakingly a degree as the others. Yeah, scattered mercenaries who usually do things like holding real seances for the living, and using information learned from the dead to con humans. Players would find them hustling humans and pay them to do something Necromancy related. Yeah, Ravnos+Necromancy could work as a reinvention of the Giovanni. Anything else overlaps so heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, or Baali that it's like, why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry about overlap if one tries to reinvent the Giovanni. With 13 Clans around and they are all vampires there's bound to be overlap. I just roll with it rather than try to fight it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T11:10:12-07:00","id":1533422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533417#post1533417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You did a good job there, I just found this part of them limiting themselves to their own family a bit forced, I find it a bit difficult to believe that the Hecata would be able to stop their members from embracing those who come from outside, the Giovanni's &quot;poison&quot; did much more sense. One idea would be to place this &quot;poison&quot; of the Giovanni as part of the promise of 1528, a guarantee that the clan would not embrace haphazardly and become enormous over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Here are some of my thoughts about family exclusivity.<br /> <br /> My version of the Giovanni aren\u2019t a Clan, they are an organization within a Clan. Maybe a Bloodline, though not necessarily mechanically so. They just happen to be such a dominant faction that in many vampire\u2019s minds they represent the Hecata. So limitations on the Giovanni embrace would not apply to the Hecata in general. So other Hecata would be around and practice diverse embracing, unlike the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Why would I want them to only embrace within the family? Because I think it\u2019s thematic. If they just embraced the best candidates, then it would just be the Hecata I\u2019m describing, it\u2019s the exclusivity which gives the Giovanni their insular mysterious flavor. I also like going with the Addams Family style dark inbred rich family, which exclusive embraces helps. If someone wants to be a Necromancer and not from the actual Giovanni family, they can play another Hecata.<br /> <br /> In my mind, this preserves the strong flavor of the Giovanni while still still allowing for diverse options. Unfortunately, I\u2019m not sure where to fit some of the other interesting Giovanni sub-families in this scenario - like the Dunsirn and Rossellini. Though, once again, given a free hand, I might just call the Giovanni the Rossellini instead, since that is an actual Italian surname.<br /> <br /> I like the Dunsirn too, I haven\u2019t figured out a way to fit them in. I don\u2019t care about the other subfamilies enough to bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T11:35:38-07:00","id":1533423,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't know if the original write-up for the Giovanni is that bad. Not for its own quality, but in a meta sense.<br /> <br /> It's easy to cite &quot;player-facing mysteries&quot; as a reason to have them gain more definition over time as the playerbase becomes more familiar with the Clan. But to a certain extent, &quot;player-facing mysteries&quot; are also mysteries to Kindred themselves, in-universe.<br /> <br /> Never forget that the World of Darkness is &quot;The World of Darkness&quot; because it's a world of conspiracies. There are a million things hiding in the shadows. Whole societies that keep their existence, much less their influence, a secret from most people. As well as secret from each other, both between splats and within them. Clan Tremere doesn't want knowledge of them and their operations getting out to either random dudes on the street, the Order of Hermes, the Sabbat, or their fellow Camarilla. Operational Security demands that every faction in the WoD keep their cards close to their chests. They aren't like the players and storytellers, who can crack open whatever book has been published and have all the Deep Lore spelled out for them.<br /> <br /> Everything else being equal, one must always assume ignorance on the part of the people (un)living in the WoD, as a default position. You must instead justify why characters know anything at all.<br /> <br /> Even as a practical matter, any given player (at least back when original WoD was going) was likely to only know what was relevant to the character they were playing. A player running a Ventrue PC would know what was in the VtM core book, and what was in the Ventrue Clan Book (whichever was available at the time). Obviously, with the Internet, all bets were off. But at least notionally, the Ventrue PC couldn't be expected to know the information found in the Malkavian or Tremere or Giovanni Clan Books. Much less in books that ranged farther afield, like the Giovanni Chronicles series. It's one of those things players needed to roleplay, their character's ignorance of deeper secrets.<br /> <br /> For this reason, one must ask what is reasonable for a common Kindred on the street to know about the Venetian corpse-f***ers. Or rather, what's reasonable for a <i>Neonate</i> to know about them.<br /> <br /> I would argue, for most PCs existing in the Camarilla, Anarchs, and Sabbat, the answer is &quot;not a whole lot&quot;.<br /> <br /> Even setting aside that information on anything more than a few centuries old is gated by a bunch of miserly Elders who see Lore as coin and have massive trust issues, Clan Giovanni is particularly out of the wheelhouse of most Kindred. They're an independent Clan that deliberately excuse themselves from the politics of the sects. They're insular and Embrace only within their mortal family (or families), so they keep a fairly tight lid on who can go blabbing all their secrets. They're functionally a crime family, so they definitely don't advertise what they do. And they're just creepy (both for the Necromancy thing, and for the Necrophilia and Incest things), so folks who know about them are reluctant to seek them out unless they have good reason.<br /> <br /> So there's very good reason to suspect the nuances of Clan Giovanni aren't common knowledge among the Neonate age bracket (by far the largest proportion of the Kindred population).<br /> <br /> Like, do the various branch families deserve mention in a hypothetical updated write-up? Probably not. Most Kindred may not realize they're Giovanni if they don't have the Giovanni name. What's a &quot;Dunsirn&quot;? Never heard of them.<br /> <br /> Is the fact Clan Giovanni were an outgrowth of Clan Cappadocian, that rose up and slew their forebears, common knowledge? Maybe not. Most Neonates are concerned enough with just navigating the Jyhad <i>as it exists presently</i>. When every scrap of information comes with a price tag in Boons, is a Neonate willing to take on more debt for what is effectively <i>trivia</i>? As far as most Kindred know, the Cappadocians are of interest only to historians. Assuming a character would even think to ask if the Clan operating tonight was not the same as has been operating since time immemorial. Most other Clans readily boast of their ancient history, even if they don't share what that history is to just anybody. Why would a Neonate think Clan Giovanni are any different? The Giovanni a Kindred is likely to meet certainly wants to appear like the scion of an ancient and established Clan, so they're not going to volunteer the information that they're only a few centuries old.<br /> <br /> The only ones likely to tell their fledglings there was a Clan BEFORE Clan Giovanni are 1) the Sabbat (who may describe them as either folks who continue to serve their Antedeluvian, or as folks who successfully killed theirs), and 2) Elders who want to badmouth the Clan as usurpers. Anything more concrete, and you'll have to start digging yourself, pay the toll in Boons, or have a Mentor knowledgeable enough and willing to spill (which the player must pay for at Char-gen).<br /> <br /> Is it common knowledge that all those Bloodlines (Samedi, Nagaraja, Harbingers of Skulls) have a connection to Clan Giovanni common knowledge? Flat no. Kindred can certainly speculate, of course. It's not a big stretch to guess at a connection. But even the books themselves have always been very vague and wishy-washy over whether anyone but the Harbingers were definitively connected by blood. (And, in the case of the Nagaraja, the books were clear no relationship exists). If even the text demurs on establishing the truth, it can be assumed it's not commonly understood in-universe.<br /> <br /> In summation, just because WE, in the Real World, know all this stuff through our collective readings of the text, doesn't mean it's common knowledge. Therefore, it doesn't make a great deal of sense to inject all that information into a write-up meant to represent what a Neonate PC is likely to know. That Clan Giovanni are a crime family that engages in business and Necromancy is already a generous allowance to most PCs who aren't, themselves, Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-31-2024, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T12:00:55-07:00","id":1533424,"title":"","content":"Great job Segreant Brother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T12:15:10-07:00","id":1533426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533401#post1533401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything else overlaps so heavily with the Ventrue, Tzimisce, or <b>Baali</b> that it's like, why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a radical alternative idea - the Baali are the Hecata. They were embraced by Asher - who is Cappadocius. What more evil Satanic Discipline can there be than enslaving the spirits of the damned? They have a propensity to use crazy inbred families as servants going all the way back to the D\u2019habi.<br /> <br /> The Cappadocians were just a bloodline that arose in Cappadocia that rejected evil and embraced Christianity. The Giovanni are just a Baali Bloodline based around a mortal family who, let\u2019s admit it, seem pretty evil and Satanic when we learn so of their practices and the goals of gathering so many souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533424#post1533424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great job Segreant Brother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 03-31-2024, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T12:56:16-07:00","id":1533428,"title":"","content":"The Baali as twisted and forgotten bloodline of the Hecate could work and some ways work better then my notion of them being a cult made up off various clan members as I was at a loss of what clan Mariah would be if we went that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T12:56:55-07:00","id":1533429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533401#post1533401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, it would be rough for me, because I disagree with the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil compared to &quot;common&quot; Disciplines like Presence and Dominate. That's an idea that works in DnD, not in VTM. And that, imo, flawed idea is extremely central to the Giovanni. If, like myself, you don't accept the idea that Necromancy is a special kind of evil, then you either have to come up with a reason for the Giovanni to be especially evil that isn't rooted in Necromancy, or jettison the idea that they are a special kind of evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what relevance this has to my post. I don't think it's necessary to view Necromancy as any more evil or tainted as any other Discipline. That certainly was not something ever intrinsic to the clan. I never mentioned that in my post. The Giovanni family was simply a modern version of the Borgias. They were supposed to be a family of corrupt, Italian merchant princes. No need to tie in an intrinsic flaw of Necromancy to how they operate. Nor to any of the other vampires in clan Cappadocian/Giovanni/Hecata. My understanding is that this is something peculiar to V5. That does not need to be part of any new clan description.<br /> <br /> We are not trying to reinvent the clan here. Just acknowledge that the &quot;Giovanni&quot; clan in fact has lots of non-Giovanni vampires in various relations to their clan's erstwhile rulers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T13:38:17-07:00","id":1533430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything else being equal, one must always assume ignorance on the part of the people (un)living in the WoD, as a default position. You must instead justify why characters know anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with that. But an 800-1000 word description of the clan is unlikely to reveal any deep seated mysteries. And many of the supposed &quot;mysteries&quot; of the Giovanni don't really seem to be all that mysterious. Simply acknowledging that the Giovanni have not, in fact, managed to kill all their predecessors or rivals within the clan is likely common knowledge.<br /> <br /> Yeah, maybe a neonate lacks a lot of specific information. But in a setting like Chicago By Night with access to elders like Critias, Tyler, Khalid, Inyanga, Nicolai, Rebekah, Lucian, and Danov - who all lived long enough when the Cappadocians still existed - there's no reason to pretend the Giovanni are this utterly unknown thing and no knowledge of the Cappadocians exist. Even younger elders that post date the Promise of 1528 are old enough to have likely met non-Giovanni vampires of the clan are talked directly with Kindred who did. Tyrus, Horace, and Annabelle probably have some knowledge.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean those characters are going to info dump the actual history in front of a PC or NPC. But I don't think many of the &quot;secrets&quot; of Clan Giovanni are in fact all that secret or unknown. Some knowledge is going to leak out, and if someone does have one of these Kindred for a Mentor, a lot of it can be given.<br /> <br /> We also don't need to treat the clan description as something that ALL neonates know. Most neonates wouldn't know the details of the Salubri bloodline description. Most of that information is only for potential players of Salubri (or perhaps the ST for use with an NPC). That's why we have the Stereotypes section of the clan description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this reason, one must ask what is reasonable for a common Kindred on the street to know about the Venetian corpse-f***ers. Or rather, what's reasonable for a <i>Neonate</i> to know about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the clan should probably be known for more than just being a small family of &quot;Venetian corpse-f***ers&quot; IMO. What's the problem with acknowledging the Samedi lineage as highly likely a surviving branch of the Cappadocians? That's even mentioned in their original 2e Vampire Players Guide blood description. Why not mention the clan was well known in the Middle Ages and earlier, and that's it's highly unlikely a small bloodline of Venetian necromancers have hunted down and destroyed the rest of the clan even with the Camarilla acknowledging Augustus as head of the clan, and that this Giovanni/Cappadocian civil war will not be interfered with by the Inner Circle and Justicars?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even setting aside that information on anything more than a few centuries old is gated by a bunch of miserly Elders who see Lore as coin and have massive trust issues, Clan Giovanni is particularly out of the wheelhouse of most Kindred. They're an independent Clan that deliberately excuse themselves from the politics of the sects. They're insular and Embrace only within their mortal family (or families), so they keep a fairly tight lid on who can go blabbing all their secrets. They're functionally a crime family, so they definitely don't advertise what they do. And they're just creepy (both for the Necromancy thing, and for the Necrophilia and Incest things), so folks who know about them are reluctant to seek them out unless they have good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are confusing the Giovanni &quot;clan&quot; with the Giovanni &quot;family&quot;. Which was the original 13 clan description. But in fact, we know that is total bullshit. There are tons of &quot;Giovanni clan&quot; vampires that aren't associated with the Giovanni family. Why pretend the Samedi aren't among them? Why ignore all these other survivors? Why not allow some new player to decide &quot;Hey, I'd like to plan a childe of one of these other vampires within the Giovanni clan that aren't part of the extended Giovanni mortal family that they are trying to hunt down.&quot; It's a perfectly valid concept. Why pretend the incredibly inaccurate clan description of 1e is anything like what would be known? That may be what actual Giovanni-Giovanni vampires want others to believe, but I think there's lots of valid reasons why there'd be other information and rumors out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, do the various branch families deserve mention in a hypothetical updated write-up? Probably not. Most Kindred may not realize they're Giovanni if they don't have the Giovanni name. What's a &quot;Dunsirn&quot;? Never heard of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they may not. The specific family names other than Giovanni may be trivial for information intended at large. But it probably wouldn't be a secret that the &quot;Giovanni family&quot; in fact is made up of several mortal families, not all of which have Giovanni as a surname. All of course would still be considered &quot;Devil Kindred&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the fact Clan Giovanni were an outgrowth of Clan Cappadocian, that rose up and slew their forebears, common knowledge? Maybe not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except even in the original description, it's publicly known that the Devil Kindred rose up and slew their forebears. Except by calling those forebears &quot;Cappadocians&quot;, there's no additional information provided. That's the main thing known about them - they're Devil Kindred who cannibalized their fellow clan mates to gain power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as most Kindred know, the Cappadocians are of interest only to historians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's actually the case. There are lots of Cappadocian survivors all over the place. In fact, if we go by the original description of &quot;only three embraced every generation&quot;, it's even possible the surviving Cappadocians outnumber the Giovanni loyalists.<br /> <br /> The idea that Giovanni somehow managed to kill all the other Cappadocians was always a weak element in the setting. We know the Salubri could be killed off because EVERY clan hunted and destroyed them. The Tremere were only the instigators to hunt down and destroy a weird, small clan. But only the Giovanni had reason to kill the Cappadocians. A small group of Venetian vampires aren't going to be able to project enough power around the world to hunt down and destroy them. The Promise of 1528 really only works if it is less than &quot;the Camarilla agreed to a genocide of the Cappadocians&quot; to &quot;Yeah, good luck with that.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533423#post1533423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it common knowledge that all those Bloodlines (Samedi, Nagaraja, Harbingers of Skulls) have a connection to Clan Giovanni common knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly a connection between the Samedi and Giovanni was speculated since the bloodline was introduced. But the mystery of that pretty much disappeared immediately. I don't think it's realistic to think people are that stupid to not put things together. I think it'd be perfectly fine to allow some doubt, but let's not pretend that's a big mystery.<br /> <br /> In terms of a new clan description, the Nagaraja would never be mentioned because they're not actually Cappadocian/Giovanni. And the Harbingers of Skulls would not be mentioned because 1) they didn't exist yet because they hadn't awakened, 2) that would be an actual example of secret lore unless/until they are introduced, and 3) there are already lots of surviving Cappadocians so their is no need to designate these as anything different from the other survivors.<br /> <br /> My basic point is that I don't see why we need to pretend much of the &quot;secrets&quot; or &quot;mysteries&quot; of the Giovanni are in fact actual secrets or mysteries. Just give an honest description of the clan as it actually existed like we do with all the other clans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T13:51:47-07:00","id":1533431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533412#post1533412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I\u2019m taking a shot at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's an excellent attempt. Maybe a little too long based on word count, but the 1000 word limit isn't a hard one.<br /> <br /> The only major things I'd likely change for my own chronicles is that 1) I'd prefer the original Cappadocian clan weakness (I'd need to mention somewhere that certain Flaws like Disease Carrier, Monstrous, and Grip of the Damned appear quite frequently in certain lineages to emulate the original various bloodline weaknesses), and 2) I'd probably change the Clan Discipline to the non-canonical Auspex, Necromancy, and Potence because of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438922#post1438922\">this discussion here</a> with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24351_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24351\" data-vbnamecard=\"24351\">Garygeneric</a> from several years ago. It combines some of the various bloodline disciplines together to sell the idea this is one clan, and I like that the Auspex + Potence combination is not had by anyone else.<br /> <br /> So I like it a lot. Wondering if we'll see anyone else make an attempt.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T15:04:41-07:00","id":1533433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533431#post1533431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's an excellent attempt. Maybe a little too long based on word count, but the 1000 word limit isn't a hard one.<br /> <br /> The only major things I'd likely change for my own chronicles is that 1) I'd prefer the original Cappadocian clan weakness (I'd need to mention somewhere that certain Flaws like Disease Carrier, Monstrous, and Grip of the Damned appear quite frequently in certain lineages to emulate the original various bloodline weaknesses), and 2) I'd probably change the Clan Discipline to the non-canonical Auspex, Necromancy, and Potence because of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1437660-5e-the-clan-updates?p=1438922#post1438922\">this discussion here</a> with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24351_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24351\" data-vbnamecard=\"24351\">Garygeneric</a> from several years ago. It combines some of the various bloodline disciplines together to sell the idea this is one clan, and I like that the Auspex + Potence combination is not had by anyone else.<br /> <br /> So I like it a lot. Wondering if we'll see anyone else make an attempt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Actually, I wanted to have the original Cappadocian Clan weakness, but I thought I was supposed to use the Giovanni weakness and Cappadocian Disciplines as per V5.<br /> <br /> I also see the appeal of a different Discipline set. It is true that Auspex and Potence is a unique combination and I like that idea. As for the Giovanni themselves, I absolutely see why they should have Potence as I imagine most of them spend time as ghouls before the embrace. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also interested in seeing other interpretations of the Giovanni, including yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T06:25:19-07:00","id":1533452,"title":"","content":"Having an Imp of Mischief giggling away on my shoulder, it<br /> may amuse the reader to know that my first response to the question of \u2018What does the average Kindred know about the Clan Giovanni?\u2019 was \u201cVampire Mafia\u201d - and to then to start laughing when I realised how very, very many factions and sub factions in the setting that could describe (Including the Ivory Tower itself).<br /> <br /> For the record, one suspects that \u2018Inbred Vampire Mafia WITH ZOMBIES\u2019 might be slightly more specific to the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, for what it\u2019s worth I quite enjoy the contrast between Clan Giovanni\u2019s utterly innocuous surname and the sheer wealth of weirdness, perverted weirdness and horror movie weirdness of the Clan itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T12:29:38-07:00","id":1533457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533452#post1533452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">t my first response to the question of \u2018What does the average Kindred know about the Clan Giovanni?\u2019 was \u201cVampire Mafia\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an issue I've gotten more cross about over the years. While I initially liked the first Giovanni clanbook (and it does have many useful things in it), I've enjoyed it less over the years mainly (but not only) because of this issue. As originally written, the Giovanni had nothing to do with gangsters. Northern Italy in general, and certainly the old Venetian Republic, had no connection with the criminal gangs of southern Italy. And the Giovanni were meant to be merchant princes of the Venetian Republic. A decadent, corrupt, and degenerate family of merchant princes, but merchant princes nonetheless. Classy, stylish, and hanging out with the cream of society with lots of sick, degenerate secrets lurking in the shadows.<br /> <br /> But because the first Giovanni clanbook was written from the perspective of some goomba Joisey-shore mafioso, the clan seemed to suddenly become a family of low class (if rich) gangsters.<br /> <br /> Now I have no problem with a sub-family like the Putanesca being a mafia family and representing clan interests in the criminal underworld. That is perfectly fine. But southern Italian organized crime gangsters should 1) have no obvious connection to the other mortal families of the Giovanni, and 2) outside those specific domains where the Putanesca family is represented, there should be little or no association with the Giovanni clan with organized crime. Northern Italian merchant princes and aristocracy, and their non-Italian allies who are likewise important merchants and financiers simply don't associate with low class thugs. Of course, there can be secret connections, and vampires in general can utilize the criminal element when needed. But it shouldn't be used to identify the Giovanni clan anymore than it does any other clan. That's not the archetype.<br /> <br /> As someone on this forum once said, &quot;Modern day Borgias&quot; should be the main concept associated with the Giovanni clan, not &quot;mafia vampires&quot;.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, I have the &quot;Putanesca crime family&quot; be one of the (mafia) Five Families of New York with interests in other cities, and many Kindred are aware of their connection to the Giovanni clan, but the Putanesca are treated as an embarrassment by the rest of the Giovanni clan. Their red headed stepchild and black sheep of the family. Useful and necessary to many clan needs, but only tolerated, kept out of clan leadership positions, and not allowed to be the face of the clan among Kindred society. That's to my taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T17:31:01-07:00","id":1533464,"title":"","content":"IMO, if you want to consolidate Clans/Lore, kinda do what Requiem did.<br /> <br /> Giovanni would be a bloodline within the Venture. It would fit the Familial Cult, banking, privateer, and merchant aspects of the clan. <br /> <br /> I think most of the latter 13 could be consolidated into the original 7 +/-2(Lasombra/Tzimisce). <br /> <br /> Giovanni seemed like Ventrue Lite to me. Necromance SEEMED powerful until a table-mate pointed out that it's a lot of extra experience spent on what Dominate/Presence to for cheaper. <br /> <br /> And for people thinking Necromancy is big bad scary evil, it only seems so when STs and Players get numb to the fact that Dominate and Presence remove individual agency and essentially turn the victim into a slave while the user generally gets a free pass on repeatedly using it. Dominate is essentially mind rape to a human. <br /> <br /> Plus the Giovanni are less numerous and have to juggle two worlds. That's twice the enemies, folks. It's just always seemed to make sense the Ventrue would beat them at everything but necromancy...and if they needed necromancers they would 'cut a deal'(read Dominate/Presence/Blood Bond) some Giovanni that were desperate/weak.<br /> <br /> So, make the Giovanni a bloodline of the Venture, remove Potence, add Fortitude, remove Presence, add Necromancy. Keep the painful feeding instead of the Ventrue weakness. <br /> <br /> As far as the Cappodocians, they rebrand into the Hecata because(handwave) the Feast only killed the Euro vamps. The Cappodocians in the Americas weren't effected. Augustus wasn't a vamp that usurped blood but rather a big time merchant mage that cut a deal with the Venture in exchange for undeath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T23:09:51-07:00","id":1533470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533464#post1533464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, if you want to consolidate Clans/Lore, kinda do what Requiem did.<br /> <br /> Giovanni would be a bloodline within the Venture. It would fit the Familial Cult, banking, privateer, and merchant aspects of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>While an interesting take, this has nothing to do with my original post. The Cappadocians/Giovanni have nothing to do with the Ventrue or any other clan.<br /> <br /> I understand someone wanting to take the basic idea of a family of merchant princes and thinking, &quot;This would be a good concept for a Ventrue character.&quot; The Ventrue are known to embrace within mortal family lineages, and it's an entirely valid concept to say, &quot;what if one of those lineages were particularly degenerate, corrupt, etc.&quot; So yes, there can be overlap. In fact, in my chronicles I do like to have Ventrue lineages of specific mortal families whose power and influence equal that of the Giovanni, and have all the intra-family intrigues the Giovanni are known for. Totally valid and lots of fun.<br /> <br /> But the Cappdocians/Giovanni/Hecata are much more than that. Concepts of a morbid obsession with death, death like visages, and other tropes particular to the CGH distinguish them from the Ventrue or any other clan. There's no reason why vampires that look more like corpses and keep to those kinds of primal tropes shouldn't be in the game. It's a good vampire archetype IMO, and the CGH is the best clan to do that. I'd like to keep those rather than just abandon the clan simply because of some (minor) overlap with the Ventrue of one aspect for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T00:40:48-07:00","id":1533471,"title":"","content":"I like Giovanni as a Ventrue/Julii bloodline, but that wouldn\u2019t be the only type of Cappadocian, it would have its own, separate origin.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade, all I\u2019d change are the mafia identity and a couple of the names (Giovanni and Puttanesca). And maybe, roll back extra-family embracing from V5; that can be a post Reunion practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:21:58-07:00","id":1533526,"title":"","content":"It would make for an interesting struggle as both the Ventrue &amp; Cappadoicans/Hecate having an interest in the Giovanni family and having to come up with some sort of agreement on what branch they could select.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T11:13:46-07:00","id":1533621,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, if you\u2019re running with the notion of \u2018Modern Day Borgias\u2019 then eventually you\u2019ll run into THE GODFATHER (Since I believe Mr Mario Puzo has been quite upfront about the Borgia influence on the Corleones).<br /> <br /> I do agree that Clan Giovanni should not be exclusively associated with \u2018Vampire Mafia\u2019 (If only because so many groups in the setting have Organised Crime elements), but I do think that the idea of the Giovanni starting out as legitimate businessmen (with some nasty skeletons in the closet) during the Renaissance and the proceeding to spend the next few centuries sinking to the level of organised crime as run by the walking dead is, if nothing else, thematically apt (A fair reflection of the profoundly toxic influence of The Beast and the difficulty of remaining tethered to Humanity in the long term).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T11:17:43-07:00","id":1533622,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the Godfather would be a pretty good inspiration for numerous vampire Clans and the Camarilla in general. The more &quot;high class&quot; mafia portrayed in the Godfather would be closer to the Giovanni than some of the more thuggish portrayals in other fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T23:23:58-07:00","id":1536934,"title":"","content":"My problem with The Cappadocians, as a whole, is that the founder is over 10,000 years old, and he still hasn't figured out the &quot;Death&quot; thing? It's pretty much a Black and White problem: Dead is dead, and live is live. But then, I ignore the whole &quot;Wraith&quot; universe, which I find unappealing.<br /> <br /> The whole motivation behind The Clan is weak, and not well thought out. And then the fantastical &quot;Well, I just need to die, and then I can eat God!&quot; epiphany after 10,000 FUCKING YEARS makes absolutely no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T23:27:35-07:00","id":1536935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533470#post1533470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While an interesting take, this has nothing to do with my original post. The Cappadocians/Giovanni have nothing to do with the Ventrue or any other clan.<br /> <br /> I understand someone wanting to take the basic idea of a family of merchant princes and thinking, &quot;This would be a good concept for a Ventrue character.&quot; The Ventrue are known to embrace within mortal family lineages, and it's an entirely valid concept to say, &quot;what if one of those lineages were particularly degenerate, corrupt, etc.&quot; So yes, there can be overlap. In fact, in my chronicles I do like to have Ventrue lineages of specific mortal families whose power and influence equal that of the Giovanni, and have all the intra-family intrigues the Giovanni are known for. Totally valid and lots of fun.<br /> <br /> But the Cappdocians/Giovanni/Hecata are much more than that. Concepts of a morbid obsession with death, death like visages, and other tropes particular to the CGH distinguish them from the Ventrue or any other clan. There's no reason why vampires that look more like corpses and keep to those kinds of primal tropes shouldn't be in the game. It's a good vampire archetype IMO, and the CGH is the best clan to do that. I'd like to keep those rather than just abandon the clan simply because of some (minor) overlap with the Ventrue of one aspect for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue and Giovanni have very much in common: they crave power, influence, and wealth. They both have Dominate as a standard Discipline. I could very much see the Giovanni as a bloodline of the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T23:57:11-07:00","id":1536939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1533470#post1533470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's no reason why vampires that look more like corpses and keep to those kinds of primal tropes shouldn't be in the game. It's a good vampire archetype IMO, and the CGH is the best clan to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never really understood the idea clans must map onto vampire archetypes, or even that the clan system is the best way of covering all the existent archetypes; it invariably seems to lead to archetypes being arbitrarily cut and trimmed to avoid thematic overlap between different clans. I wouldn't advocate <i>merging</i> clans in order to have them better fit established archetypes\u2014the Ventrue, the Lasombra and the Giovanni are individually more interesting to me than a singular Bela Lugosi clan would be\u2014but I think it'd be wise to avoid the excessive proliferation of clans. Given that looking and behaving like a living corpse is a trait shared by more than one kind of vampire, I'd rather have the 'Giovanni look' be achieved through a <i>mechanic</i> than a designated clan\u2014is becoming corpselike not already stated to be a consequence of low Humanity?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think merging Giovanni with the Ventrue would be misguided! If anything, having them be the most distinguished family among the Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> would be a better fit; having two separate clans based on Southern European stereotypes seems like something of an overkill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T13:02:44-07:00","id":1537025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1536939#post1536939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really understood the idea clans must map onto vampire archetypes, or even that the clan system is the best way of covering all the existent archetypes; it invariably seems to lead to archetypes being arbitrarily cut and trimmed to avoid thematic overlap between different clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a gimmick that allows players to quickly decide what kind of character they want to play. Certain clans lend themselves to certain kind of characters. You can always create a character that goes against archetype, but that too is an advantage because it leads to certain kind of interactions with other members of the clan.<br /> <br /> There's no problem with different lineages of vampires essentially being the same, but that doesn't really provide any hook for players (or the ST) to latch on to. It would make clan choice irrelevant and make a lot more work for the ST to distinguish NPCs from one another. It's just an artifact of being an RPG. And I think it's a major reason why VtM proved so successful. Around the time Vampire came out, there were several RPGs that allowed people to play monstrous characters like Nightlife and Nightbane, but the World of Darkness line won out over them for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1536939#post1536939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't advocate <i>merging</i> clans in order to have them better fit established archetypes\u2014the Ventrue, the Lasombra and the Giovanni are individually more interesting to me than a singular Bela Lugosi clan would be\u2014but I think it'd be wise to avoid the excessive proliferation of clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not disagree with you. The original seven Camarilla clans are pretty much all that one needs. Yes, the game always intended to have thirteen clans. But the four independent clans were obviously intended as limited antagonists that served the setting in particular ways as opposed to broad based archetypes. The Assamites were simply intended to be a group of vampire assassins that anyone could hire or be targetted by. The Setites were worms that would eat the apple from within. The Giovanni were untrustworthy merchants you could deal with, but had their own agenda. Ravnos were meant to provide a rival to the Gangrel in the wilderness. The Lasombra and Tzimisce existed simply to provide the Sabbat unique clans to it. Little thought was really given to distinguishing them other than their intended role in the setting combined with a unique Discipline. <br /> <br /> Revised and later editions attempted to broaden these clans to varying success. Some good things were done to make them more interesting and believable, but by V5 the main result has been to make certain clans unrecognizable from what they originally were.<br /> <br /> I certainly found the many bloodlines to be excessive, and their unique Disciplines seemed to be making vampires more like a superpowers game than a game about vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1536939#post1536939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that looking and behaving like a living corpse is a trait shared by more than one kind of vampire, I'd rather have the 'Giovanni look' be achieved through a <i>mechanic</i> than a designated clan\u2014is becoming corpselike not already stated to be a consequence of low Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the clan weaknesses are not meant to be unique takes for each individual line. They are usually just more pronounced takes on general vampire weaknesses. All vampires have to make Self-Control checks, but the Brujah make theirs with a penalty. Any vampire can have a Derangement, but the Malkavians all have a permanent Derangement that cannot be removed. All vampires intake blood whose different types provide different value of &quot;nutrition&quot; and often have a particular style of hunting, but the Ventrue have stricter requirements. All vampires take damage from sunlight, but the Setites take even more damage. The Cappadocian weakness is just a stronger version of the normal rules for vampire appearance. Some clans do have a distinctive weakness (like the Nosferatu and Lasombra) that do not really affect other vampires, but these are usually represented by Flaws that can be given to any vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T05:36:32-07:00","id":1537147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1536934#post1536934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with The Cappadocians, as a whole, is that the founder is over 10,000 years old, and he still hasn't figured out the &quot;Death&quot; thing? It's pretty much a Black and White problem: Dead is dead, and live is live. But then, I ignore the whole &quot;Wraith&quot; universe, which I find unappealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense to this position but even without Wraith, dead is dead and live is live is a weird track to take when you're a walking corpse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole motivation behind The Clan is weak, and not well thought out. And then the fantastical &quot;Well, I just need to die, and then I can eat God!&quot; epiphany after 10,000 FUCKING YEARS makes absolutely no sense. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the larger question is why it didn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T22:06:16-07:00","id":1537193,"title":"","content":"I go with that Cappadocius went somewhat insane over the ages and perhaps misread what he saw in his visions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T20:07:35-07:00","id":1537289,"title":"","content":"Well the first thing I'd do is give the Brujah Necromancy to go with their Carthaginian death cult roots, and to give them some magic to justify their name (likely given after the clan scattered for the Carthaginian colonies on the southern coast of Spain). <br /> <br /> Then I'd just make the Giovanni into Brujah -- a very tightly knit, insular group of Brujah with a very powerful familial head who diablerized his sire.<br /> <br /> I'd set them in Trieste, not in Venice. <br /> <br /> I know, that sounds eerily specific. Almost as if that's what I actually did for my games... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T09:14:36-07:00","id":1537307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533399-how-would-you-rewrite-the-original-giovanni-clan-description?p=1536934#post1536934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with The Cappadocians, as a whole, is that the founder is over 10,000 years old, and he still hasn't figured out the &quot;Death&quot; thing? It's pretty much a Black and White problem: Dead is dead, and live is live. But then, I ignore the whole &quot;Wraith&quot; universe, which I find unappealing.<br /> <br /> The whole motivation behind The Clan is weak, and not well thought out. And then the fantastical &quot;Well, I just need to die, and then I can eat God!&quot; epiphany after 10,000 FUCKING YEARS makes absolutely no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see this as a plot hole. Characters, in-narrative, are <i>allowed</i> to be wrong. They're <i>allowed</i> to be driven by hubris to pursue senseless goals. Indeed, it would be weird for a 10,000 year old super-vampire with vast knowledge of life and death to NOT fall prey to hubris. That's okay, narratively speaking. (Especially if you frame it as his Tragic Flaw that brings about the downfall of his Clan.)<br /> <br /> Moreover, does a Clan NEED to have a Clan-wide motivation? I don't think it's necessary. It's <i>useful</i>, sure, but they don't all need to be on the same page. Their theme just needs to be strong enough for more general vampire motivations to bounce off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T14:23:10-07:00","id":1537318,"title":"","content":"People need to understand that the clans are not monolithic and are comprised on indidivual people with there own goals and it would conflict with others in the &quot;family&quot; A member of the Ventrue greatest problem is not a member of the Brujah, Lasombra or Tzismce clans who might fight them on rulership, but it would be a fellow clan mate who wants your spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}